# Gurbalib game content

New game content belongs in `lib/domains/<area>/` unless you are modifying a base class in `lib/std/`.

## Domain layout

```
lib/domains/<area>/
  rooms/       # Room .c files
  monsters/    # NPC .c files
  objects/     # Items, weapons, armor, furniture
  weapons/     # Optional area-specific weapons
  armors/      # Optional area-specific armor
```

Register the area with `add_area("areaname")` in each room's `setup()`.

## Rooms

```lpc
inherit "/std/room";

void setup(void) {
   add_area("myarea");
   set_short("Short description");
   set_long("Long description, can span " +
      "multiple quoted strings.");
   set_exits(([
      "north" : "/domains/myarea/rooms/north_room.c",
      "south" : "/domains/other/rooms/entry.c",
   ]));
}
```

- Exit values are **absolute paths** to `.c` files
- Optional: `set_dark_msg()`, `set_light()`, `set_weather()`, `set_pk()`, `add_item()`, `set_commands()`
- See `lib/doc/help/wiz/room_code` and `lib/domains/required/rooms/start.c`

## Monsters

```lpc
inherit "/std/monster";

void setup(void) {
   set_name("goblin");
   add_adj("nasty");
   set_short("A nasty goblin");
   set_long("It glares at you.");
   set_gender("male");       /* male, female, unknown — or omit for random */
   set_race("goblin");       /* looks in /domains/required/objects/races */
   set_level(5);
   set_hit_skill("combat/unarmed");
   set_skill("combat/unarmed", 50);
   set_skill("combat/defense", 100);
}
```

- Equipment: `set_wearing("/path/to/armor.c")`, `set_wielding("/path/to/weapon.c")`
- Behavior modules: inherit or use `m_wander`, `m_actions`, `m_aggressive` patterns from `lib/std/modules/`
- See `lib/doc/help/wiz/monster_code` and examples in `lib/domains/2.4.5/monsters/`

## Objects (items, weapons, armor)

- Items: inherit `/std/object` or a specialized base (`/std/weapon`, `/std/armor`, `/std/container`)
- Always implement `setup()` to set `set_id()`, `set_short()`, `set_long()`, and relevant properties
- Use modules for behavior: `m_wieldable`, `m_wearable`, `m_readable`, `m_openable`, etc.
- See `lib/doc/help/wiz/object_code`

## Races

Race definitions live in `/domains/required/objects/races/`. `set_race("name")` loads the matching race file.

## Content guidelines

- Keep descriptions in plain in-character prose; use `%^COLOR%^` codes sparingly for ANSI color
- Use existing areas and objects as templates before inventing new patterns
- Do not hardcode player names or wizard-specific logic in domain objects
- Test by cloning with wizard `clone /domains/...` and placing with `update` + `goto`
